From: Tetraeder
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: mul_mat_id treats expert id -1 as no expert

As the CPU kernel does: no weights read, zero output row. MMVQ and MMVF write the zero row in the
kernel; MMQ and MMF never match -1 to an expert and a small kernel zeroes its rows; the generic
fallback gathers from a zero row. mm_ids_helper counts -1 below every expert, which leaves the
first compact rows and the -1 slots' inverse-map entries unwritten; MMQ's quantize kernels read
src1 or scatter through them, so they now point at row 0. Results for ids without -1 are
unchanged. ADR 0070.
---
